SERVICES

All Digital Venturis models come standard with a three-year warranty. Year
one features on-site service and years two and three are return-to-Digital
service. This warranty represents one of the most comprehensive in the
industry and includes product lifetime toll-free technical assistance,
bulletin board, automated fax, and one year of technical support for
software purchased with the system.

TECHNICAL DATA

Microprocessors

Venturis 433sx		i486SX/33 MHz (slimline only)
Venturis 450s2		Am486 SX2/50 MHz (slimline and full-profile)
Venturis 466		Am486 DX2/66 MHz (slimline and full-profile)
Venturis 4100		IntelDX4/100 MHz (slimline and full-profile)
Venturis 560		Pentium 60 MHz (slimline only)

Coprocessor

Integer math/numeric capabilities are integral to Am486 SX2/50 MHz, Am486
DX2/66 MHz, IntelDX4/100 MHz, Pentium 60 MHz, Intel SX2, Intel DX2, and
IntelDX4 OverDrive Processors.

Microprocessor Cache

The i486SX/33, Am486 SX2/50 MHz, Am486 DX2/66 MHz systems feature 8 KB of
on-chip primary cache memory. The IntelDX4/100 MHz and Pentium 60 MHz
microprocessors feature 16 KB of on-chip primary cache memory. All Venturis
486-based models can be upgraded with 128 KB of direct-mapped write back
secondary cache. Venturis 560 models feature 256 KB of direct-mapped
write-through secondary cache standard.

System Memory

Venturis 486-based systems feature models with 4 or 8 MB of RAM, expandable
to 68 MB using industry-standard 4, 8, 16 or 32 MB 70ns non-parity SIMMs.
All Venturis 486-based models feature two industry-standard 72-pin SIMM
sockets. The 4 MB models have 4 MB of non-parity system memory surface
mounted on the system board. The 8 MB models have 4 MB of non-parity system
memory surface mounted on the system board and one 4 MB SIMM installed in
bank 1.

Venturis Pentium 60 MHz systems feature models with 4 or 8 MB of RAM,
expandable to 64 MB using industry-standard 4, 8, 16, or 32 MB non-party
SIMMs. All Venturis Pentium 60 MHz models feature two industry-standard
72-pin SIMM sockets. The 4 MB models are configured with a 4 MB SIMM
occupying bank 0, and 8 MB models are configured with a 4 MB SIMM in bank 0
and in bank 1.

Expansion Slots

Venturis slimline 486-based models feature three industry-standard 16-bit
expansion slots: two full-size 16-bit ISA slots and one 16-bit half-size ISA
slot. Venturis 60 MHz Pentium models feature three industry-standard
expansion slots: one full-size 16-bit ISA; one full-size PCI/ISA slot; and
one half-size PCI slot.

Venturis full-profile models feature five industry-standard 16-bit expansion
slots: four full-size 16-bit ISA slots and one 16-bit half-size ISA slot.

Enhanced Local Bus IDE

All Venturis slimline and full-profile models feature dual channel enhanced
local bus IDE. This allows each model to support up to four IDE devices (two
high speed devices on the local bus channel and two devices on the ISA bus
channel) plus connectivity to hard disk drives with storage capacity greater
than 528 MB.

Device Bays

The Venturis slimline models feature two externally accessible device bays:
one 3.5" device bay occupied with a standard 2.5-inch, 1.44 MB diskette
drive and one open/available 5.25-inch x 1.0-inch high bay; and two internal
3.5-inch x 1.0-inch high hard disk drive bays (hard drive models have one
bay configured with standard IDE HDD and one open/available hard disk drive
bay).

The Venturis full-profile models feature three externally accessible device
bays: one 3.5-inch device bay occupied with a standard 3.5-inch 1.44 MB
diskette drive, two open/available 5.25-inch x 1.0-inch high bays, and two
internal 3.5-inch x 1.0-inch high hard disk drive bays (hard drive models
have one bay configured with standard IDE HDD and one open/available hard
disk drive bay); and one device bay designed for an optional PCMCIA/IR
device supporting two Type I/II or one Type III PCMCIA adapter providing
seamless connectivity to Digital Mobile computing products.

Diskette Drives

All Venturis models come standard with a 3.5-inch 1.44 MB diskette drive,
and feature optional industry-standard 5.25-inch 1.2 MB floppy and 3.5-inch
2.88 MB diskette drives.

Hard Disk Drives

Digital Venturis models feature 270 MB and 540 MB IDE hard disk drives,
providing ample storage for data and applications. The local bus IDE
interface speeds data to and from the hard disk drive at the speed of the
system clock.

