GIGAswitch/ATM Joins Family of High Performance Network Switches

HIGHLIGHTS

o  High performance ATM switch for LAN backbones and high performance
   workgroups

o  Provides high capacity: up to 52 155 Mbits per second SONET/SDH ports

o  Robust networks through FLOWmaster flow control

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The GIGAswitch/ATM system is a high performance ATM switch especially suited
for use in LAN backbones and in high performance workgroups. The initial
product supports up to 52 155 Mbits per second SONET/SDH multi-mode fiber
ports, using a 10.4 Gbits per second switch fabric. Within the next six
months, support will be extended to other media (single-mode fiber and
unshielded twisted pair Category 5 wiring), T3, E3, and 622 Mbits per second
NET/SDH.

Permanent Virtual Circuits and Switched Virtual Circuits are supported, as
are Constant Bit Rate (CBR), Variable Bit Rate (VBR), and Available Bit Rate
(ABR) traffic.

FLOWmaster flow control eliminates cell loss for ABR traffic, providing a
robust network for bursty data traffic. The GIGAswitch/ATM system will also
support the ATM Forum's forthcoming specification for rate-based flow
control.

A GIGAswitch/ATM switch can be managed by any SNMP compliant network
management application, including the POLYCENTER NetView product. The switch
may also be managed through an out-of-band management interface via a Telnet
session.

BENEFITS

o  High performance -- 10.4 Gbit per second switch fabric, with SWITCHmaster
   enabling over 95 percent utilization.

o  Robust networks -- No cell loss due to congestion with FLOWmaster flow
   control.

o  Guaranteed quality of service -- Support for Constant Bit Rate and
   Variable Bit Rate traffic, with user-defined latency limits.

o  Simplified network management -- Autoconfiguration, reconfiguration, and
   dynamic routing of virtual circuits dramatically reduce the amount of
   effort needed to operate an ATM network.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The GIGAswitch/ATM products are available now through local Digital sales
offices and through Digital business partners (packaged with implementation
services or application specific solutions). Volume availability will occur
in February 1995.

The GIGAswitch/ATM chassis (DAGGA-CA) includes the crossbar switch module
and the clock/management card. It does not include a power supply. Order at
least one power supply (two if redundancy is desired).

If users anticipate that they will use more than 10 linecards in the switch
(the switch has a capacity of 13 linecards), the following should be
ordered:

o  DEFGB-DA/DB GIGAswitch 20 amp power supply [quantity one]
o  DEFGB-BA GIGAswitch 48V power supply [quantity two]

If users expect to use 10 or fewer linecards in the switch, any of the
following may be ordered:

o  DEFGB-AA/AB GIGAswitch (15 amp) power supply [quantity one]
o  DEFGB-BA GIGAswitch 48V power supply [quantity one]
o  DEFGB-DA/DB GIGAswitch 20 amp power supply [quantity one]

Order the power cord for each DEFGB-AB. Model numbers are DEFGX-A*/B*,C/*.
Power cords for the the U.S. model, the DEFGB-AA, are included with the
power supply.

Order the power cord for each DEFGB-DB. The power cord for the U.S. model,
DEFGB-DA, is included with the power supply. Order numbers are listed in
this article.

Order redundant power supplies (and power cords for non-U.S. versions) as
necessary. Order the appropriate number of linecards (DAGGL-AA). Each
linecard has four 155 Mbits per second SONET/SDH multi-mode fiber ports
integral to the card.

