SERVICES

Users are encouraged to purchase the product with Standard Warranty.
Standard Warranty includes same-day onsite service (DSMC), plus 24 hours,
seven-day-a-week telephone support. Digital takes responsibility for problem
isolation and onsite repair of the GIGAswitch/ATM, all within a matter of a
few hours.

Under list warranty, users are required to isolate problems to the failing
field replaceable unit (FRU), call Digital to receive a Return Authorization
(RA), mail the failed FRU to Digital, and install the replacement FRU into
the GIGAswitch/ATM. This scenario has an overall problem resolution time of
several days. List warranty should only be considered for users who are
technically proficient with the product, require limited technical support,
and do not mind the turnaround time needed to receive a replacement part.

Digital product installation services are available and are recommended. The
installation price covers installation of the entire system (chassis, power
supplies, linecards, and PMDs). Installation prices are also available for
options added to the system subsequent to initial install. Users who are not
trained and experienced with the product are strongly encouraged to have
Digital do the installation. Digital installation will save time and money.

TECHNICAL DATA

The GIGAswitch/ATM system provides 10.4 Gbits per second aggregate bandwidth
in a 13 x 13 nonblocking crossbar switch. The SWITCHmaster parallel
iterative matching algorithm prevents head-of-line blocking in the switch
fabric, resulting in over 95 percent utilization of the switch fabric.

Q.2931 signalling is used to establish Switched Virtual Circuits. (Permanent
Virtual Circuits are also provided.) Constant Bit Rate (CBR) and Variable
Bit Rate (VBR) traffic, as well as Available Bit Rate (ABR) traffic are
supported.

FLOWmaster flow control provides zero cell loss for ABR traffic. In the
future, the GIGAswitch/ATM system will also implement explicit forward
congestion indication (EFCI), in support of the ATM Forum's forthcoming
specification for rate-based flow control.

High availability is provided through:

o  Redundant power supplies and connections to an external battery or power
   source
o  Redundant fans
o  Ability of each linecard to be "master" and failover in the event of a
   failure in the elected master
o  Hot swap capability of fans, power supply, and power system control
o  Hot swap capability of the linecards (through a firmware upgrade after
   initial shipments of systems)

The GIGAswitch/ATM system can be managed by any SNMP-compliant network
management application, including the POLYCENTER NetView application. SNMP
MIBs and agents are provided with the GIGAswitch/ATM hardware. The switch
may also be managed through an out-of-band management via a Telnet session.
Future updates to the firmware will be downline-loadable.

The GIGAswitch/ATM platform has 14 slots, with one of those slots reserved
for management functions.  The other 13 slots are for use by linecards. The
first linecards available for the system have four 155 Mbits per second
SONET/SDH multi-mode fiber ports (integral) per card, providing a maximum of
52 ports. A later version of the linecard will provide support for daughter
cards that support a variety of media (155 Mbits per second SONET/SDH on
multi-mode fiber, on single-mode fiber, and on UTP Category 5, plus T3 and
E3).

The switch is mountable in a standard 19-inch communications rack. Both AC
and DC power are available, with redundancy an option. Air plenums allow
units to be "stacked" with no extra clearance.

Devices that connect to the GIGAswitch/ATM ports must comply with the ATM
Forum's UNI V3.0. SC connectors are used.


