Easy Upgrade to X.25 V1.0a for OpenVMS AXP

HIGHLIGHTS

o  X.25 V1.0a for OpenVMS AXP systems can be installed using DEC X.25 Client
   for OpenVMS AXP key

o  Upgrading is easy and cost effective

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Upgrading systems from DECnet systems to DECnet/OSI systems is now easier.
Users who are running the DEC X.25 Client with DECnet for OpenVMS AXP
systems can upgrade without the cost and inconvenience of purchasing a
second product license.

Digital offers two software products enabling connection of OpenVMS AXP
systems to packet-switching data networks (PSDNs) conforming to CCITT X.25.
They are X.25 V1.0a for OpenVMS AXP (SPD 47.37) for DECnet/OSI systems and
DEC X.25 Client V1.1 for OpenVMS AXP (SPD 46.37) for DECnet Phase IV
systems.

Both products support all of the following:

o  Process-to-process (X.25 network service) communication
o  Process-to-terminal (X.29) communication
o  Terminal-to-process (X.29) communication
o  DECnet/OSI Connectionless Network Service
o  DECnet/OSI Connection Oriented Network Service
o  X.25 mail
o  Switched or Permanent Virtual Circuit communication (up to 4096 per
   system)
o  X.25 connection accounting and security
o  Network management and troubleshooting using the Network Control Language
   (NCL) and Common Trace Facility (CTF)

The DEC X.25 Client is limited to use with an X.25 gateway or relay node to
provide access to an X.25 PSDN. The client is only supported when used with
DECnet for OpenVMS AXP systems.

The X.25 for OpenVMS AXP product is a full functionality implementation for
systems running DECnet/OSI software. It includes serial synchronous
communications interface device driver support, allowing direct connection
of the system hardware to a PSDN, as well as the utilities and application
programming interfaces of the DEC X.25 Client product.

New Features

With this update of X.25 for OpenVMS AXP systems, users who are licensed for
the DEC X.25 Client product can use their existing Client Product
Authorization Key (PAK) to install the full function X.25 product. The delay
and cost associated with the purchase of a second license and use of a
separate PAK is no longer necessary.

For users employing the DECnet and DEC X.25 Client products, upgrading the
OpenVMS AXP system to using the DECnet/OSI product is easier than ever. The
DECnet PAK will install DECnet/OSI software, and the Client PAK will install
X.25 for OpenVMS systems. (Note that only upgrading will work; the DEC X.25
Client product cannot be installed using the X.25 for OpenVMS PAK.)

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

X.25 V1.0a for OpenVMS AXP systems is available now. Media and documentation
kits for both products listed below are supplied on the August 1994 OpenVMS
Layered Product CD-ROM. Hard copy documents are also available. New features
for this release of X.25 for OpenVMS AXP systems have been documented in the
Release Notes.

