PATHWORKS V5.0 for OS/2

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Support for IBM OS/2 V3.0 and IBM LAN Server 4.0

o  Runs DECnet based Microsoft Windows applications on OS/2

o  OS/2 Lotus Notes servers can be incorporated into PATHWORKS networks

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

PATHWORKS V5.0 (SPD 55.24.06) for OS/2 software allows OS/2 workstations to
participate in DECnet Phase IV networks as end or nonrouting nodes. OS/2
workstations can be connected to OpenVMS systems, OSF/1 systems, Windows NT
systems, or OS/2 systems, and can use selected resources and services of
those systems.

The PATHWORKS V5.0 for OS/2 software supports the latest releases of the
OS/2 operating system as well as network operating systems from IBM and
Microsoft. PATHWORKS V5.0 layers on valid retail configurations of either
the IBM LAN Server or Microsoft LAN Manager to provide greater flexibility.

The PATHWORKS V5.0 software provides DECnet support to OS/2 systems
configured as either clients or servers. PATHWORKS V5.0 for OS/2 includes a
DECnet virtual device driver that will permit DECnet based PATHWORKS for DOS
and Windows DECnet based applications to run on OS/2 client systems.

BENEFITS

o  Users can run 16-bit, DECnet based Windows applications on OS/2 V2.1
   system using the DECnet Virtual Device Driver provided in PATHWORKS V5.0
   for OS/2. Examples of DECnet-based applications include:

   - TeamLinks Mail V2.5 for Microsoft Windows
   - TeamLinks Office V2.5 for Microsoft Windows
   - PATHWORKS for VT320 terminal emulator

o  SETHOST, a terminal emulator that supports multiple LAT and CTERM
   sessions is provided. The SETHOST terminal emulator now runs in an OS/2
   Window rather than in full-screen mode. This includes a scripting
   facility for automation of frequently executed functions.

o  PATHWORKS V5.0 for OS/2 includes license management software. The
   software allows the client to communicate with PATHWORKS license and file
   servers for obtaining and using PATHWORKS client-based licenses.

o  The addition of LAT V5.1 permits applications on host and server systems
   to access printers connected to client PCs. LAT sessions can be connected
   to printers or to PC communication ports. Both PC communication ports and
   printers may be advertised as LAT services by the client PC. It is also
   possible to configure the LAT printer services advertised by the client
   PC.

o  Users will experience an easy upgrade process. The upgrade process to new
   versions of PATHWORKS software has been simplified with an automated
   removal process. The PATHWORKS V4.1 for OS/2 software is detected and
   associated files are automatically removed prior to installation of
   PATHWORKS V5.0 for OS/2.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

PATHWORKS V5.0 for OS/2 software is available now through local Digital
sales offices and business partners. Listed below are PATHWORKS part numbers
for client-based licenses. Refer to the online Customer Update article,
"PATHWORKS Licensing Practices" in the October 25, 1993 issue for
explanations of the new PATHWORKS licensing options.

Only one copy of the media and documentation kit is required per network,
including the FPA media kit. PATHWORKS V5.0 license part numbers were
available with shipment of PATHWORKS V4.1 for OS/2. If you already purchased
a PATHWORKS V5.0 license, then only a media and documentation kit is
required to run PATHWORKS V5.0 software.

