TECHNICAL DATA

PATHWORKS V5.0 for OS/2 runs on Intel platforms (386, 486, Pentium).
PATHWORKS V5.0 requires 2 Mbytes of memory in addition to requirements for
the OS/2 operating system and the selected network operating system.

PATHWORKS V5.0 for OS/2 will run on Intel 286 processors only on OS/2 V1.3.
This restriction is due to the OS/2 V2.x operating system that does not
support Intel 286 processors.

PATHWORKS for OS/2 product now supports the latest operating system and
network operating system from either IBM or Microsoft. The PATHWORKS V5.0
for OS/2 release layers on valid retail configurations supported by either
vendor:

o  OS/2 server configurations
   - IBM OS/2 V3.0 and LAN Server V4.0
   - IBM OS/2 V2.11 and LAN Server V4.0
   - IBM OS/2 V2.1 and LAN Server V 3.0
   - Microsoft OS/2 V1.3 and LAN Manager V2.2

o  OS/2 client configurations
   - IBM OS/2 V3.0 and LAN Server V4.0
   - IBM OS/2 V2.11 and LAN Server V4.0
   - IBM OS/2 V2.1 and LAN Manager V2.2
   - IBM OS/2 V2.1 and LAN Requester V3.0
   - Microsoft OS/2 V1.3 and LAN Manager V2.2

PATHWORKS V5.0 only supports features consistent with support in the
underlying operating system and network operating system. For example,
Microsoft OS/2 V1.3 does not support Virtual Device drivers. Therefore, the
DECnet Virtual Device Driver provided in PATHWORKS V5.0 for OS/2 will not
run on Microsoft OS/2 V1.3.

Due to the limitations in Microsoft OS/2 V1.3, PATHWORKS V5.0 for OS/2 will
be the last release to provide support for Microsoft OS/2 and Microsoft LAN
Manager. Users committed to OS/2 should migrate to IBM OS/2 and IBM LAN
Server.

Users deploying OS/2 as an interim measure in a migration to Windows NT may
decide to remain with Microsoft LAN Manager V1.3 and LAN Manager V2.2 for
OS/2 despite its limitations -- Microsoft LAN Manager for OS/2 V2.2 only
supports IBM OS/2 V2.1 as a client system. The DECnet Virtual Device Driver
will not work.

PATHWORKS for DOS/Windows (LAN Manager) clients will interoperate with IBM
LAN Server.

