TeMIP V2.0 Product Set for DEC OSF/1

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Telecom network management product on DEC OSF/1 platform

o  Integrated solution for heterogeneous, multi-vendor, multi-protocol
   networks

o  Unique set of core applications based on telecommunications standards for
   fixed wire and mobile networks

o  Off-the-shelf solution and development environment

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The TeMIP product set is based on an open, modular, and object oriented
architecture implemented in a flexible client/server manner. This allows the
development and deployment of distributed, hierarchical network management
solutions: the TeMIP framework (i.e., POLYCENTER Network Manager 200
[formerly known as DECmcc Basic Manager System] functionalities porting onto
DEC OSF/1 systems).

TeMIP software is a unique set of core applications based on standards such
as OMNIpoint 1 (Network Management Forum recommendations), ISO's OSI
(International Standards Organization's Open System Interconnect), and
ITU-TS (Telecommunications Network Management recommendations for public
networks).

The applications include:

o  TeMIP Alarm Handling --  Allows for the management of ISO formatted
   alarms information (a specific type of event in ISO terminology),
   enabling users to define comprehensive alarm filtering, realtime
   monitoring, and recording.

o  TeMIP Event Logging -- Enables users to define single or multiple
   collection and recording of events for a domain that represents the
   entire or selected portions of the network.

o  TeMIP Trouble Ticketing -- Enables the initiation and efficient
   coordination of network problem solving and maintenance activities.

The TeMIP products allow users to create additional applications and
integrate them into a framework to form a customized network management
solution. Access module (AM) and functional/presentation module (FM)
development toolkits are available to users to enable quick development of
customized modules for Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) or ASCII/TL1
equipments. Toolkits include:

o  TeMIP OSI Management Toolkit -- Provides for the access to the OSI
   Q3/CMIP environment in accordance with Telecommunications Management
   Network (TMN) recommendations. It provides the means to maintain and
   manage Guidelines for the Design of Managed Objects (GDMO) models of
   managed objects and integrate them into the TeMIP runtime environment
   without any production activities disruption, thanks to the GDMO Model
   Maker. It uses the standard and commercially available XMP API to access
   TMN Q3 stack.

o  TeMIP ASCII Management Toolkit -- Provides for the access to elements
   that do not support standardized management interfaces but still use
   ASCII type messages, thus providing access to legacy systems.

o  TeMIP Framework Development Toolkit -- Allows developers to define and
   customize presentation or functional modules.

This integrated solution addresses the needs for heterogeneous, multi-vendor
and multi-protocol networks, including the management of traditional
equipment with non-standard protocols. It is this flexible, customized
approach that provides network users and operators with an advantage.

TeMIP Framework V2.0 Features (SPD 54.17.00)

o  Support of two major SQL database management systems -- ORACLE and INGRES
   -- has been added for the TeMIP Trouble Ticketing, Alarm Archiving, and
   TeMIP Framework Exporter FM applications.

o  Allows the integrated definition of user profiles with access control
   rights from domain and application levels to the entity class instance
   and its associated attributes and to the verb (directive) and its
   associated arguments.

o  Logging of Operator's Commands (LOC) that allows defined operator actions
   to be stored in a database and thus available for future analysis and
   processing.

o  The TeMIP Security Toolkit allows for the integration of an access
   control mechanism in any newly developed management module or application
   that makes use of TeMIP services.

o  Fully localizable through its built-in OSF/1 XPG4 standard compliance and
   support.

o  Iconic map usability (e.g., zooming and sizing, lookup to top domain,
   automatic TeMIP applications startup, and color customization for lines
   and texts within maps).

o  Support of ISO values of alarm types and probable cause fields in the
   alarm FM.

o  Generation of ISO formatted alarms in SNMP AM (e.g., IP reachability,
   incoming traps, and enterprise-specific traps).

o  Surveillance of PM connection to an operation context, to know whether
   operation contexts are monitored and by whom.

o  Launch of external applications from the Trouble Ticketing application.

Migration to TeMIP V2.0

It is strongly recommended that ULTRIX users upgrade their systems, as TeMIP
V1.1 and PNM200 V1.3 products are in end-of-life mode.

BENEFITS

o  Foundation for building service management solutions. A set of core
   applications and object oriented architecture allows development and easy
   integration of new applications.

o  Based on international standards. Standards compliance ensures that the
   investments made today will not become obsolete in a matter of few years.

o  Provides unified view of the network for end-to-end service solution.
   With a "manager of managers" approach for an integrated network
   management system, older management systems can be retained while new
   state-of-the-art technology is introduced. A single view of the network
   can be presented with a consistent user interface to reduce operator
   errors and training requirements. Its open management software system
   design provides the foundation for end-to-end network and service
   management, and ensures the fast introduction and management integration
   of diverse technologies such as SDH/SONET, ATM, and GSM/IS.41.

o  Protects investment in legacy network management and operation systems.
   Besides the support of international standards, it is equally important
   to be able to interconnect with proprietary protocols, interfaces, and de
   facto standards. The TeMIP product's architecture through the concept of
   access modules allows integrating the management of all sorts of network
   elements, legacy systems, and applications as well as ASCII/TL1 devices.

o  Provides superior security and performance. A high level of security is
   essential to all telecom operators, especially if service management
   capabilities are extended to corporate network users. For example, the
   ability of the user to manage service defaults and call routing functions
   on a free phone application. It also provides the high level of
   performance required by telecom networks through software design and the
   superior performance of Alpha technology. TeMIP products can manage tens
   of thousands of network elements spread throughout the world.

o  Saves development costs and allow for growth. The ability to grow
   flexibly and quickly when required by increased capacity and funded by
   the associated revenues should be a critical selection criteria. Access
   module development toolkits and APIs allow both the loose integration
   (launching from the user interface) of existing building blocks or
   applications and the incremental development and implementation of
   tightly coupled management functions in a seamless manner.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

TeMIP V2.0 is available now through local Digital sales offices. The TeMIP
product set uses a traditional flat license.

