FVS30 FDDI Storage Server for OpenVMS Clusters and FDDI Networks

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Storage server allows disk storage devices to be served in an OpenVMS or
   Alpha cluster environment

o  Optional ZVR42 controller provides SCSI failover and controller based
   RAID 0, 3, and 5 for the  high availability typically associated with
   VMSclusters

o  Users can select from several FDDI options, including the award winning
   GIGAswitch product

o  Server supports very high capacity storage requirements (capacity ranges
   beyond one Tbyte)

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The FVS30 FDDI Storage Server allows for disk storage devices to be served
in a VAX or Alpha cluster environment for users who prefer FDDI because of
its high performance and ability to support long distances.

Based on high performance AlphaGeneration technology, the FVS30 comes with
one DAS FDDI port and one thinwire Ethernet port. Additionally, there are
five TURBOchannel slots, each of which supports up to seven Single-Ended or
Fast Wide Differential (FWD) SCSI-2 devices, for a maximum of 35 devices.

The FVS30 may not serve as a boot node to a VMScluster. Its primary purpose
is to serve user data to other members of the cluster or to networked
clients via TCP/IP or PATHWORKS software.

Several FDDI interconnect options are available from Digital, including
DECconcentrator 500 for small clusters, DEChub 900 for medium-sized
clusters, and the GIGAswitch product for large or high performance clusters.

The FVS30 can be connected to a StorageWorks cabinet via the HSZ40, or
StorageWorks disks can be mounted in a standard Digital cabinet using BA350
shelves.

Controller Option for High Capacity and SCSI Disk Failover

For high capacity requirements, a ZVR42 controller is available with the
FVS30. Each ZVR42 supports up to 24 RZ28 disks, for a total configuration of
840 disks or greater than 1.5 Tbytes of disk storage capacity. Additionally,
the ZVR42 provides controller based RAID 0, 3, and 5 as well as SCSI disk
failover. When the FVS30 is configured in a dual server configuration with
redundant controllers, all connected SCSI disks will failover to the backup
server.

FDDI Storage Server for Disaster Recovery and Backup Performance

The FVS30 FDDI Storage Server supports several tape devices for backup and
archive, including the Digital Linear Tape (DLT) family (TZ86, TZ877) and
TL820 Automated Tape Library. An FVS30 can be placed in a remote location up
to 40 km (about 28 miles) away from the datacenter for support of remote
vaulting and disaster recovery. Tape drive failover and Tape Mass Storage
Control Protocol (TMSCP) serving to other cluster nodes is not supported at
this time.

The FVS30 also supports backup and archive software such as VMS BACKUP and
Storage Library System (SLS). For best backup performance, the FVS30 should
be configured to back up local disks to local tapes, thereby eliminating
backup traffic from the cluster interconnect. This can significantly reduce
backup times in cases where the cluster interconnect is the bottleneck for
backup performance.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The FVS30 FDDI Storage Server is available now through Digital's sales
offices and business partners. Custom configuration analysis is required and
delivery is approximately 60 days after receipt of order.

TECHNICAL DATA

All VMScluster clients must operate OpenVMS VAX V5.5-2 or higher, or OpenVMS
AXP V1.5 or higher. All clients in an FDDI VMScluster will be Mass Storage
Control Protocol (MSCP) served.


