o  Supports Hewlett-Packard 9000 series 700 and 800 systems

o  Supports IBM RS/6000 systems

o  Supports Intel systems running Windows NT

o  Modular, flexible storage solutions

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The StorageWorks architecture provides unprecedented flexibility in
configuring desktop, deskside, and even departmental storage solutions.
Many users today are standardizing on a storage architecture for all vendor
platforms in their enterprise. With the announcement of HP and IBM support,
StorageWorks products now support a wide variety of vendor and operating
system platforms including: Novell, Sun Solaris, SunOS, MS-DOS, UNIX, HP-UX,
IBM AIX, Windows, and Windows NT.

HP and IBM product support includes disk, tape, and CD-ROM storage devices,
plus the complete line of StorageWorks enclosures. These products have
undergone extensive testing in each vendor's environment to ensure
compatibility.

An extensive line of StorageWorks products is also now available for Intel
and Windows NT users. Supported products for Intel systems running Windows
NT include the RAID Array 210, 8mm, 4mm, and DLT tape drives, disk drives,
and CD-ROM drives.

The RAID Array 210 offers Windows NT users cost effective high availability
for PC networks. It was announced in July 1994 for use on Novell systems and
has received an excellent response.

IBM and HP users can now expand their workstations with the StorageWorks
"pizza box" or deskside pedestal and add up to 14 Gbytes of external
storage. The StorageWorks departmental cabinets are also available to
provide from 120 to 240 Gbytes of rackmounted storage for larger systems.

