Storage Library System V2.4a for OpenVMS VAX and AXP

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Supports OpenVMS AXP V6.1 systems and mixed VAX and AXP clusters

o  Tx877 tape loader support as either random slot or sequential stacker

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Storage Library System (SPD 29.67) continues to deliver on the need to
cost effectively manage the time consuming and difficult task of backing up
data on OpenVMS platforms. V2.4a introduces support for OpenVMS AXP V6.1 and
offers continued support for OpenVMS V1.5 in AXP or mixed VAX and AXP
clusters, as well as for standalone systems. This enables the migration from
pure VAX to mixed VAX and AXP environments, taking advantage of AXP
performance, while preserving expertise gained with Storage Library System
on VAX systems. V2.4a also supports Tx877 magazine loader devices in either
random slot or sequential slot selection mode.

For more information, see the "Storage Library System (SLS) for OpenVMS
V2.3" article in the February 15, 1993 issue of Customer Update.

BENEFITS

Users who have built their automated backup upon Digital's Storage Library
System are adding OpenVMS for AXP V6.1 systems to their clusters. This
release allows for the incorporation of these systems into the Storage
Library System environment, with no operational paradigm changes. Other key
benefits include:

o  "Set and Forget" policies and support for unattended operations that save
   system management time and expense.

o  User-based file restoration that improves user productivity and lowers
   system management costs.

o  Increased data integrity and security by ensuring that backups occur
   automatically per policy and that copies of vital corporate data are
   maintained.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Storage Library System V2.4a is available now. Storage Library System is
sold in a client/server arrangement. Users are required to have at least one
Storage Library System server license in their network. Client licenses are
called SLS REMOTE. Storage Library System also supports the StorageTek ACS
4400 silo. The Storage Library System ACS license is used for this purpose.

Product services for SLS REMOTE and SLS ACS are included in SLS product
service, and SLS REMOTE and SLS ACS media and documentation kits are
included in the SLS kits.

