software installed. A media kit with a replication license is available to
provide cc:Mail V2.0 functionality to clients. This license need only be
purchased once as the software can be used for multiple installations.

The cc:Mail Connection for MailWorks provides an upgrade from cc:Mail
LAN-based file-sharing technology to MailWorks client/server messaging,
without requiring a change to the user interface. By adding the cc:Mail
Connection software, clients will have access to additional menu options for
MAILworks services.

Basic mail operations include: create and delete folders; send, read,
create, delete, and copy messages; attach text and binary files; reply to
and forward messages; search; and specify filtering rules.

Distributed Directory Services (DDS) are provided by MailWorks servers via
MAILbus Services (VAX Messager Router/DDS or DEC X.500 Directory Service) as
is connectivity to all other MAILbus gateways and complementary products in
the enterprise system. A personal address book is also available, with
support for free-form addressing.

