KAP Supports Parallel Programming for DEC OSF/1 Systems; Windows NT

HIGHLIGHTS

o  SMP support for DEC OSF/1 systems, offering automatic and directed
   decomposition of Fortran 77 and C programs

o  Support for Alpha platforms running Microsoft's Windows NT

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

SMP Support for DEC OSF/1 Systems

Users with compute-intensive codes that would benefit from the additional
processors on an SMP system need a way to decompose their codes to run
across the processors.

In response to this need, Digital has extended its KAP language preprocessor
offering to support the parallel decomposition of Fortran 77 and C languages
-- the most popular languages used in compute intensive applications. KAP
V2.0 provides both automatic and directed decomposition of programs. With
the automatic decomposition feature, the preprocessor will analyze an
existing program to locate loops that are candidates for parallel execution,
and will then decompose the loops. KAP V2.0 takes care of creating shared
data and synchronizing access to that data.

In addition, a programmer can use KAP software in a guided automatic mode,
by inserting assertions and directives to guide the language preprocessor in
the decomposition of individual loops. The software also supports the
Parallel Computing Forum (PCF) directives for manual decomposition of
programs.

The KAP preprocessor still performs all of its usual serial code
optimizations, including:

o  Advanced memory management
o  Data blocking for cache
o  Complete suite of loop transformations
o  Extensive support of inlining
o  Annotated program listings

While every program will not benefit from KAP software's parallel
decomposition and optimization functions, these represent additional value
for users.

KAP Support for Windows NT

Digital has also extended its KAP language preprocessor offering to support
Alpha systems running Microsoft's Windows NT operating system. KAP V1.0 for
Windows NT software will provide a set of powerful program analysis,
inlining, and optimization features that improve program performance and
programmer productivity.

Versions are available for both Fortran and C languages. The Fortran version
is designed to interoperate with DEC Fortran for Windows NT, and the C
version is designed to operate with the Alpha version of the CL compiler
supplied with the Windows NT Software Development Kit (SDK).

The combination of Digital's Alpha technology, with its impressive
computational performance, and Windows NT software, with its ease of use and
powerful features, is attracting users away from traditional engineering
workstations. As users and developers start moving codes from workstations
to PCs, they will need the same high quality language products they used on
their workstations.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

KAP software versions supporting DEC OSF/1 SMP, Windows NT, and OpenVMS AXP
systems are available now.

