DECathena System Management Consulting Services

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Fixed price and custom quote services

o  Multivendor solution

o  For DECathena software running on ULTRIX, DEC OSF/1, HP, Sun, IBM, SGI,
   and Windows platforms

SERVICE DESCRIPTION

Digital's DECathena solution was developed to address several problems
associated with large UNIX and PC distributed environments, including the
high cost of client/server management, unenforceable network security, and
complex multivendor integration. DECathena services integrate the best
aspects of mainframe computing with the power and flexibility of client/
server computing. A range of services is offered to meet the diverse needs
of each user.

DECathena Comprehensive Site Assessment Service

Comprehensive Site Assessment Service includes an in-depth business and
technical analysis of a user's IT environment. This service is delivered in
two phases. Phase 1 consists of gathering site information from one or two
people in each of the departments that will be directly affected by the
project. Phase 2 involves creating a report, which covers the following
areas:

o  Estimated cost of the DECathena implementation
o  Benefits analysis
o  Preliminary project schedule and milestones
o  Desired end state

The site assessment report includes:

o  Executive Summary
o  Technical Analysis
o  Implementation Proposal
o  Exhibits

DECathena Implementation Starter Service

This service is designed for users who have purchased DECathena licenses for
implementation at one location. During this service, a Digital specialist
will design the DECathena environment, and will install and configure the
DECathena service on 2 servers and 28 clients.

This service is delivered in three phases:

Phase 1:  A brief site assessment is carried out to design how the DECathena
          service will be implemented. This phase is documented in a report.

Phase 2:  A DECathena implementation plan is developed.

Phase 3:  Two DECathena servers and 28 clients are installed and configured.
          In addition some acceptance testing is performed, and users will
          be oriented for further deployment of the DECathena environment,
          according to its design and implementation plan.

Note: Software license cost is extra.

DECathena Implementation Service

This service provides for custom implementation of a secure, manageable,
client/server infrastructure using repeatable solution components. A site
assessment of some form is typically a prerequisite to Implementation
Services. If the site is suitable, an implementation project plan is
created. Detailed implementation planning is undertaken based on information
obtained from the site's assessment. The complete DECathena Services
installation is performed, followed by acceptance testing and user
orientation.

The Implementation Service includes the installation, project management of
the installation, initialization, and proof-of-connectivity of the DECathena
environment. These are typical deliverables for the Implementation Service:

o  Statement of Work (SOW) -- A typical SOW addresses training,
   documentation, installation, DECathena operations and demonstration,
   warranty, and Update Service.

o  Complete installation.

o  Any custom service needed per the SOW.

DECathena Proof of Concept Service

This service is designed for users who want to evaluate a DECathena
implementation in their own environment. The purchase of DECathena licenses
is not required for this service, as it includes the loan of the software
for one server and 10 clients for a period of 90 days.

There are three deliverables:

o  A brief site assessment is carried out to design how DECathena services
   can be implemented at the site. This phase is documented in a report.

o  A DECathena Implementation Plan is developed.

o  One DECathena server and 10 clients are installed at one site and
   configured for a period of 90 days. Direct Internet and phone support
   from DECathena engineering are provided for 90 days.

decathena application migration service

this service evaluates and integrates existing applications and makes them
client/server ready. this service provides a complete application analysis
that identifies potential problem areas and makes recommendations to resolve
these problems. this service may require custom software service to make
applications client/server ready.

The Migration Service focuses on:

o  Applications needing modifications.
o  Applications needing reconfiguration.
o  Rearrangement of application installation.
o  New mechanisms to automate application installation.

DECathena Custom Software Service

This service custom engineers the software for users for implementation of
DECathena. Creation of additional DECathena client software on platforms not
covered by base product is also provided as a service.

Digital provides programmers and project managers to customize applications
into a distributed environment so that the application can take advantage of
the security features of DECathena services (Kerberos security) and other
features such as messaging (Zephyr Message Service).

DECathena Custom Training Service

This service teaches users concepts beyond those taught in "Introduction to
DECathena Services and Basic System Management." It includes hands-on,
onsite training for system administration personnel and end users. This
training gives personnel a comprehensive understanding of the operation of
their new distributed computing environment and related tools in their
realtime operational setting. The intent is to assure complete familiarity
and ease of use and to accelerate full productivity.

DECathena Single Sign-On Solution

For users, a multiple hardware and operating system environment looks like
one system from log on to log off. The Single Sign-On Solution is able to
handle a vast combination of hardware and operating systems and maintain a
high level of security.

The Single Sign-On Solution includes three components:

o  Technology architecture
o  Custom engineering
o  Consulting service

The Single Sign-On service begins with a comprehensive assessment of the
existing environment and user requirements. From this, a Single Sign-On
integration plan is developed and presented.

BENEFITS

DECathena System Management Consulting Services provide users with the
expertise to get started in the right direction, faster implementation, and
gives them more time for day-to-day operations.

