DECevent Service Tool

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Maximizes OpenVMS AXP system availability through pre-notification and
   diagnosis of hardware problems

o  Enables users to schedule maintenance activities at their convenience

o  Automatic notification to Digital when service on hardware is required

o  Complementary to users with hardware service contract or equivalent
   warranty coverage

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

DECevent software tool, the newest Digital service tool, predicts certain
classes of hardware failures, provides the solution, and enables scheduled
maintenance. The tool extends many of the predictive maintenance advantages
of Digital's VAXsimPlus tool to the OpenVMS AXP environment. It provides
automatic monitoring and analysis of AXP system hardware components with
notification to the user that service is needed before a problem is actually
experienced. Additionally, if desired by the user, service calls can be
logged automatically to Digital (with a copy to the user) with no
intervention or effort on the user's part.

Notification includes identification of the failing hardware (to the user
and Digital) and recommendation of what service action is required (to
Digital). The results are proactive, planned maintenance. Users can schedule
their downtime when it is convenient for them, improving their application
availability and end user productivity.

BENEFITS

o  Application availability and planned maintenance -- DECevent enables
   users to reallocate system resources to prevent interruption of
   operations and to schedule maintenance at their convenience.

o  Automatic service call logging -- At a user's discretion, service calls
   can be logged automatically to Digital, with no effort on the user's
   part.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The DECevent service tool is available now. OpenVMS AXP users with a
multivendor hardware services contract or warranty may obtain the advantages
of DECevent software tool by contacting their local service delivery office,
which will order the service tool and make installation arrangements.

TECHNICAL DATA

DECevent V1.1A is available today for AXP systems (non-PC), running a
minimum of OpenVMS AXP V6.1, and will be available in the near future for
DEC OSF/1 systems.

