OSI Application Developer's Toolkit V2.2

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Toolkit available on OpenVMS AXP system

o  Continuing support on OpenVMS VAX, DEC OSF/1, and ULTRIX RISC platforms

o  Includes OSI ASN.1 compiler, OSI TP, application and presentation
   interface, and FTAM APIs

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The OSI Application Developer's Toolkit enables users to write distributed
applications that communicate over an OSI network. The toolkit uses services
provided by DECnet/OSI systems.

This toolkit allows for the development of applications on OSF/1, OpenVMS,
or ULTRIX operating systems. For applications that are intended to run on
all systems, source code must be compiled and linked with the toolkit on
each operating system. The toolkit is required on the development system and
the compile/link system. The resulting application can be run on any
DECnet/OSI system with the appropriate operating system. The toolkit is not
required on these target systems unless the application is using ROSE or OSI
TP. The toolkit supports APIs for the following OSI services:

o  File Transfer, Access, and Management (FTAM) services as defined by ISO
   8571
o  Association Control Service Element (ACSE) and presentation layer
   services as defined by ISO 8650, 8649, 8823, and 8822
o  Abstract Syntax Notation One (ASN.1) tools as defined by ISO 8824 and
   8825
o  OSI TP (Transaction Processing) as defined by ISO 10026
o  Remote Operations Service Element (ROSE) as defined by ISO 9072

Platform Support

The toolkit is available on OpenVMS, DEC OSF/1, and ULTRIX platforms. The
chart below shows which APIs and tools are provided on each platform.

                     OpenVMS AXP    OpenVMS VAX	   DEC OSF/1   ULTRIX
Toolkit Version	     2.2            2.2	           2.2         1.1

FTAM		     Yes	    Yes		   Yes	       Yes
ACSE/presentation    Yes	    Yes		   Yes	       Yes
ASN.1 compiler	     Yes	    Yes		   Yes	       No
ROSE		     No		    Yes		   Yes	       Yes
OSI TP		     Yes	    Yes		   Yes	       No

BENEFITS

o  ASN.1 compiler -- Removes the need for user written encode and decode
   routines.

o  OSI TP -- Provides powerful yet flexible program-to-program interface.

o  Consistent APIs for OpenVMS, ULTRIX, and DEC OSF/1 platforms -- Allows
   for lower cost of development across platforms.

o  Programming access to OSI upper layer services -- OSI services allow the
   development of multivendor distributed applications.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

OSI Application Developer's Toolkit V1.1 for ULTRIX systems and V2.2 for
OpenVMS AXP and DEC OSF/1 systems are available now. V2.2 for OpenVMS VAX
systems will be available in January 1995.

