PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The MailWorks for OpenVMS mail system has a flexible and scalable
client/server design that supports a full range of user environments from
small workgroups to full enterprise solutions. Heterogeneous desktops and
legacy mail systems can be integrated for smooth communication across the
enterprise.

MailWorks software provides a choice of mail clients, including TeamLinks
for Windows and Macintosh, Microsoft Mail for Windows, Lotus cc:Mail for
Windows, DOS, and Video Terminals. Layered on top of Digital's VAX Message
Router, MailWorks software interacts with all other MAILbus gateways and
complementary products.

New License Options

New license options for concurrent users have been added, effective February
24, 1995. Concurrent user increments of 1 user, 25 users, 50 users, and 100
users are available with prices that make these options attractive for large
and small configurations. Prices and license options are identical for VAX
and Alpha systems.

Support for OpenVMS AXP

MailWorks for OpenVMS V1.3 is available on Alpha systems. Early performance
testing shows a 300 percent increase in the number of users supported on
comparable systems using V1.2. MailWorks for Video Terminals will be
supported on both Open VMS VAX and AXP platforms. Support for MailWorks for
DEC Windows software is available for OpenVMS VAX systems only.

Lotus cc:Mail Client Support

MailWorks for OpenVMS V1.3 includes built-in support for direct use of Lotus
cc:Mail for Windows clients, transforming the PC LAN file sharing
environment of the cc:Mail for Windows V2.0 user into a client/server
messaging technology that provides dependable, secure, and robust mail
services. The conversion to the MailWorks Server is transparent to users,
who continue to use cc:Mail in the same manner. Additional menu options are
available to access services provided by MailWorks software, such as a
personal address book and Distributed Directory Services with VAX Message
Router, as is connectivity to all other MAILbus gateways and complementary
products in the enterprise system.

To use cc:Mail with MailWorks software the client PC must have both cc:Mail
V2.0 installed (not provided with the cc:Mail Connection) and the MailWorks
cc:Mail Connection. A separate media kit and replication license is
available for this purpose. This kit can be used by every cc:Mail desktop
that will connect to the MailWorks Server.

The cc:Mail Connection for MailWorks provides an upgrade from cc:Mail LAN
based file sharing technology to MailWorks client/server messaging without
requiring a change to the user interface. Additional menu options provide
access to the services of the MailWorks product.

Basic mail operations include: Create and delete folders; send, read,
create, delete, and copy messages; text and binary attachments; reply and
forward messages, search, and rules.

