Transarc's Encina on DEC OSF/1

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Transarc's Encina Distributed TP Monitor available for DEC OSF/1
   platforms

o  Encina extends the OSF DCE to support the development, execution, and
   management of medium to large-scale, multiplatform, client/server
   applications

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Encina for DEC OSF/1 platforms is Transarc Corporation's implementation of
its Encina distributed transaction processing products on Digital's Alpha
platforms under the DEC OSF/1 operating system. Encina for DEC OSF/1 systems
extends the services of the OSF DCE to provide a platform for developing,
executing, and administering distributed transaction processing systems. It
supports a three-tiered architecture for medium to large-scale,
mission-critical, client/server applications. The Encina for DEC OSF/1
products include Encina Base Services, Encina Server Core, Encina Monitor,
Encina Structured File Server, Encina Recoverable Queuing Service, and the
Encina Peer-to-Peer Communications Executive. In addition, Transarc also
separately offers Encina for Windows, a PC-based client for the Encina
Monitor.

BENEFITS

o  Powerful and flexible programming environment to deal with a range of
   application requirements.

o  Modular architecture to allow selection of just those components required
   for a given application.

o  Tight DCE integration to take full advantage of the power of DCE.

o  Provides IBM host connectivity.

o  High performance in a distributed environment to support medium to
   large-scale client/server applications.

o  Designed for scalability to meet the needs of growing businesses.

o  Common Encina and DCE administation to simplify the management of
   distributed transaction processing applications.

o  Available on more than 15 different platforms to ensure a consistent
   Encina programming environment across the multivendor platforms typical
   of today's businesses.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Encina for DEC OSF/1 systems will be available from Transarc in December
1994. Encina follows a tiered pricing model (i.e., the price of an Encina
for DEC OSF/1 license is generally a function of the specific class of
hardware platforms on which the product is installed). The definition of the
following tiers is consistent with the definition used by Digital for its
own products.

Encina Base Services
Encina Server Core
Encina SFS
Encina RQS
Encina Monitor
Encina C Development Tools
Encina COBOL Development Tools
Encina PPC Executive
Encina Media and Manual
Encina Annual License Fee

For application developers and pilot projects, Transarc offers Encina
"QuickStart" bundles -- consisting of binary licenses, media, documentation,
training, and support -- at substantial discounts. Contact Transarc for more
detailed information.

Licensing Information

The purchase and use of Transarc Encina for DEC OSF/1 systems is managed
through software licenses. Encina for OSF/1 systems uses the Network License
System (NetLS), part of the future OSF Distributed Management Environment
(DME), to facilitate license management. Encina software modules request
licenses for use when they are invoked, and software licenses are granted as
available by machines running the NetLS server software.

All of the Encina modules (except the Encina Application Development Tools)
are licensed per machine (e.g., a machine with a valid license to run the
Encina Base Services can support any number of Encina applications, Encina
servers, and Encina users that require the use of this module). Encina for
DEC OSF/1 systems uses "floating" licenses, so each license for a particular
Encina module can be used by any machine on the network that needs to run
that module. The number of machines that can run a given Encina module
concurrently is limited only by the number of licenses purchased, and when
an individual machine is finished with a license, it becomes available for
use by other machines.

The Encina C Application Development Tools are licensed per user -- each
concurrent user of the Encina Application Development Tools requires a
separate license. Multiple concurrent users on a single machine require
separate licenses.

The Encina COBOL Application Development Tools are licensed per user -- each
individual user of the Encina Application Development Tools requires a
separate license. Multiple users on a single machine require separate
licenses.

SERVICE

Transarc Corporation offers Encina and DCE Application Development
consulting services to help users implement solutions based upon DCE and
Encina. In addition, Transarc regularly offers both DCE and Encina user
training classes at its Pittsburgh headquarters and periodically at other
locations around the world. These classes may also be given on-site.

TECHNICAL DATA

Encina for DEC OSF/1 systems is layered on and requires Digital's DCE
services for OSF/1. All machines in the Encina environment must run both the
DCE Base Services and the Encina Base Services, and there must be at least
one DCE Cell Directory Service and one DCE Security Service in the
environment.

