RoboMon and RoboCharge Automated Management Tools

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Heroix' RoboMon and RoboCharge automated systems management tools

o  Rule-based automated systems monitoring, problem detection, and remedial
   action

o  Customizable functions for monitoring rules and reporting

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Heroix's RoboMon and RoboCharge products are now available for OpenVMS VAX
and AXP systems. They are layered software products that help automate
systems management tasks. RoboMon provides a rule-based problem detection
and management system to monitor a running system and carry out tasks based
on system events and conditions. RoboCharge helps automate the labor
intensive process of user accounting, project accounting, and usage
chargeback.

RoboMon enables system management and operations staff to automate a variety
of operational tasks, including problem detection and resolution, remote
site management, and centralized event monitoring. A performance option
allows dynamic systems performance monitoring, tuning, and reporting.

Rule-based Technology

RoboMon is driven by a rule-based engine that monitors for conditions and
takes actions based on the found conditions. The basic automation system
includes a set of predefined operational sensors to automate tasks. The
sensors monitor and react to common systems and operations problems. All
sensors are self-configuring so no special set-up is required -- either when
the software is installed or when changes are made to the system
configuration. All sensors are adjustable for thresholds, selection of
entities to monitor, notification, and whether to take corrective actions.
Cool-off periods and escalation policies also are supported.

The rule development option allows new rules to be defined using an
English-like rule definition language, enabling users to define their own
conditions and actions based on site-specific situations. RoboMon also has a
performance option with expert-level rules that analyze performance on an
ongoing basis and provide detailed advice regarding the specific nature of
performance problems. Tuning advice can be optionally implemented based on
the observed performance.

All areas of OpenVMS performance are covered, including CPU performance,
I/O, memory, paging, and clusterwide issues. A variety of reports and graphs
to help the system manager monitor performance on an ongoing basis also is
produced.

RoboCharge

RoboCharge is a resource, project accounting, and chargeback system for
OpenVMS and UNIX systems. RoboCharge operates in a single node, cluster, or
network configuration. The system collects resources used and storage usage
data following user-defined policies. These policies define the level of
detail the data is maintained at; the times of the day that the data is
collected; and the disk devices from which to collect storage data.

BENEFITS

o  Efficiency -- RoboMon's automation provides for systems monitoring and
   problem management for more systems with the same or fewer staff members.
   RoboCharge collects and reports systems usage and accounting with less
   staff time.

o  Improved service -- RoboMon can assist in detecting problems earlier than
   would otherwise be possible. In many cases where users have specified
   automated remedial actions, RoboMon can help remove problems directly,
   thus improving service delivery and overall systems availability.

o  Increased resource utilization -- Performance management options help
   detect and repair system problems that would otherwise reduce user
   satisfaction and user response times.

PRODUCT POSITIONING

RoboMon complements Digital's POLYCENTER offerings by providing rule-based
technology for problem analysis and resolution. In addition, RoboMon can
operate in a standalone or peer-to-peer environment, and hence does not
require network operation to continue its problem management functions.

RoboCharge provides a comprehensive set of usage accounting that allows
consolidation across OpenVMS systems as well as collecting usage data from
selected UNIX systems.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

RoboMon and RoboCharge are available now through local Digital sales
offices. The RoboMon Full and Performance options for OpenVMS AXP systems
will be available sometime within the first half of 1995.

RoboMon and RoboCharge are licensed from Heroix and priced by system class
for both Alpha AXP and VAX systems. RoboMon Full Kit includes both the
RoboMon Rule Development System and RoboMon Performance options. RoboMon
Automation contains only a fixed set of system monitoring rules and may be
suitable for more limited situations.

