NetCon for ManageWORKS V2.2

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Lower costs for PC LAN management

o  PC LAN asset management -- hardware and software inventory, software
   distribution, software metering, license control, configuration control,
   troubleshooting tools, and remote control

o  "Out of the box" integration with PATHWORKS ManageWORKS

o  All management of any PC can be done from any PC on the LAN

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Digital and CapaCity Inc. relationship represents the first in a series
of partnerships forged to combine and integrate the NOS-centric PC LAN
management strengths of PATHWORKS ManageWORKS with the strengths of PC LAN
System Management application software vendors. NetCon's PC Lan Asset
Management Software now contains a built-in interface to ManageWORKS
software. System managers now will be able to manage the NOS in their LAN
and the assets in their LAN from a single console.

NetCon V2.2 software includes an integration module for ManageWORKS
software. ManageWORKS software is the management framework tool for
Digital's PATHWORKS product. The module allows end users to use the NetCon
console from within the ManageWORKS console, while also deploying the
ManageWORKS navigation tools and display facilities.

PATHWORKS V5.0 for DOS and Windows client software includes ManageWORKS
software. This allows PC network managers to view and manage essential
aspects of a network operating system directly from a remote PC through a
single, advanced graphical user interface. Using ManageWORKS software, the
PC system manager can manage PATHWORKS servers, retail LAN Manager (V2.x),
and NetWare (V2.x, 3.x) servers, configure PATHWORKS clients remotely and
simultaneously view and manage multiple servers and clients.

Using NetCon, the PC LAN system manager can automatically generate a
hardware inventory database that contains information about RAM, CMOS,
processor type, bus type, hard disk data (including disk space), ports,
device drivers, TSR software, memory overview, network adapter types,
Ethernet addresses, and station addresses.

PC system managers also can create their own database fields in NetCon. Data
can be detected and collected automatically into these fields. All
information is detected, and transferred to the central NetCon database.
History information is saved for comparison purposes and used for
troubleshooting PCs in the system.

NetCon also performs software inventory based upon an industry standard
relational database format whereby information about the software installed
on each PC is automatically detected and collected. This information can be
used to summarize information about groups of PCs, register the approved
number of licenses for individual products, and see which PCs have installed
or de-installed various products over a period of time.

Software metering information in NetCon shows concurrent use of any software
product, can be summarized for groups of PCs, and also can be used to lock
out users from a software product, if the number of approved licenses for
the product is exceeded.

NetCon's user defined configuration control centrally stores several
versions of  configuration files such as CONFIG.SYS, AUTOEXEC.BAT, WIN.INI,
and SYSTEM.INI. It is possible to change the data in the configuration files
stored in the database and transfer a new version back to the PC. The
different versions of a configuration file can be compared with previous
versions, for troubleshooting purposes. Colors are used to focus
configuration changes.

NetCon's software distribution allows automatic software distribution to an
individual, a group, or all users. Forced or optional software distribution
is performed by executing a script created by the PC LAN system
administrator. Additional tools are provided with the system to make the
creation of software distribution scripts easier.

BENEFITS

NetCon helps users control their PC LAN costs by helping them manage their
PC hardware and software inventories. It also helps reduce costs for the
installation, upgrade, and configuration of PC software. NetCon helps
schedule forced or optional software distribution, enforce software
licensing policies, and troubleshoot and fix PC problems.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

