LSF V2 Load Sharing & Distributed Batch Software for UNIX Networks

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Enables Alpha systems, along with other vendors' installed systems, to
   form heterogeneous UNIX clusters

o  New features include easy-to-use graphical user interfaces, job
   checkpointing and migration, non-shared file systems and Andrew File
   Systems, PVM software, and extensive job statistics

o Included in AdvantageCluster Compute Systems and TechAdvantage software
   packages

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

As the computing demands of enterprises escalate and computing budgets are
constrained, networked UNIX computers are used increasingly for mission
critical applications. To replace mainframes, these UNIX clusters must have
the same features as the larger systems, such as sophisticated batch queuing
systems, system management and monitoring tools, and checkpoint, restart,
and migration. Features such as transparent load balancing, batch and
interactive load sharing, parallel processing, and the ability to make
machines from various manufacturers work as one are necessary to replace
supercomputers. UNIX operating systems generally do not supply these
features.

To help users meet their downsizing needs, Digital has teamed with Platform
Computing Corporation to offer LSF, the Load Sharing Facility. LSF is
distributed load sharing and batch queuing software that transforms the
network into a shared computing resource by providing a transparent, single
view of all hardware and software resources, regardless of platform
differences. LSF works for both interactive and batch jobs, plus it contains
support for parallel packages such as PVM and HPF. LSF V2.0 supports all
major UNIX platforms, including DEC OSF/1, ULTRIX, IBM AIX on RS 6000
systems, HP-UX on HP 9000 systems, SGI IRIX, SunOS and Solaris on Sun
SPARCstations, and ConvexOS on C-series supercomputers.

V2.0 is the first major release of LSF since its introduction in 1992. This
release builds upon the ground breaking technology established by earlier
versions and offers these new features:

o  Simplified installation and administration -- LSF V2.0 provides a set of
   scripts for installing and upgrading LSF with minimal effort.

o  Personal load sharing -- Single-user mode of operation is installable by
   an ordinary user without the system administrator's help. This is useful
   for personal productivity gains and for easy trials.

o  A suite of graphical user interfaces -- LSF V2.0 provides graphical user
   interfaces for batch processing and system load monitoring integrated
   into a single framework and based on the X Motif standard.

o  Support for checkpointing and migration -- LSF V2.0 provides a checkpoint
   library for all supported platforms, and can automatically checkpoint
   user jobs and migrate them to less loaded hosts. Checkpointing at kernel,
   user, and application levels is fully integrated.

o  Support for non-shared file systems and Andrew File System -- With LSF
   V2.0, all computers on a network can share all their jobs without having
   a shared file system. Transparent remote file access facilities are built
   into LSF V2.0.

o  Improved system management and monitoring tools -- LSF V2.0 manages
   floating licenses for application software and provides extensive job
   statistics, accounting, and monitoring capabilities for both interactive
   and batch jobs.

o  Mainframe-like batch processing -- LSF V2.0's support for job dependency,
   configurable execution conditions, full job and event logging, extensive
   job control mechanisms, and ultra-high reliability provides
   mainframe-class batch services.

o  Parallel processing tools -- LSF V2.0 supports all major parallel
   application packages, including PVM and HPF, along with sophisticated
   scheduling algorithms for multiprocessor and parallel jobs.

o  Site configurable arbitrary system information collection -- LSF V2.0
   allows a site to configure up to 21 external load indices that provide
   arbitrary information about the participating hosts to be used in LSF's
   job scheduling. LSF V2.0 ensures optimal job placement in heterogeneous
   systems environments through a rich network resource requirement
   specification language.

o  LSF clients -- An LSF client host has transparent access to all LSF
   utilities without having to run any server. This eases administration and
   reduces cost of ownership.

o  Expanded license options -- In addition to the LSF server licenses
   offered in past releases, there are now client licenses and SMP licenses.
   Client licenses are appropriate for slow or minimally configured systems.
   No daemons or load-shared jobs run on clients. However, all load-sharing
   utilities are available on the client to transparently ship jobs to
   servers for execution.

BENEFITS

o  Greater user productivity through shorter interactive response time and
   higher batch job throughput.
o  Better utilization of computing resources.
o  Shared environment for all interactive, batch, and parallel workloads.
o  Reduced user concerns for heterogeneous systems and for availability of
   applications on every platform.
o  Capability for processing larger jobs through parallel computing.
o  Simplified use and management of UNIX networks.
o  Total control of computing resource sharing to implement site policies.
o  Ability of incremental upgrade to add the most suitable new systems.
o  Tracking system usage to eliminate bottlenecks.
o  Open environment for growth and customized applications.

Each user in the system, regardless of what is on the desktop, has access to
a virtual supercomputer. Administrators and managers can do their jobs
better through effective management, better utilization of corporate
computing resources, and more flexibility in system upgrades. These benefits
currently are being realized at LSF sites with thousands of networked
computers.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

LSF V2.0 is available now for all supported platforms. LSF V2.0 also is
included in AdvantageCluster Compute Systems and TechAdvantage software
packages.

LSF software is offered under the terms and conditions of Platform Computing
Corporation. Documentation in the QB order numbers does not refer to user
