POLYCENTER AssetWORKS V1.0

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Point-and-click hardware and software inventory, plus drag-and-drop
   electronic software upgrades

o  Help desk, remote control, and remote boot of PCs

o  Automated management reports, including system inventory, installed
   software, and job history

o  Online tutorial for getting started and context sensitive help for online
   assistance

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

POLYCENTER AssetWORKS software provides the practical solution for
automating configuration and asset management tasks for the broad range of
platforms across the enterprise network. It facilitates the collection of
hardware and software configuration data, automates the distribution and
installation of applications and software upgrades, and provides remote
control of PCs -- getting it all under control for today's system manager.

All management functions can be performed from a single console using a
Windows NT graphical user interface, and the solution scales seamlessly from
the single PC LAN to the worldwide enterprise.

Features

o  Centralized management of the enterprise, with distributed local control
   for remote branches or departments. POLYCENTER AssetWORKS software
   supports whichever paradigm the user wants to use when running the
   business.

o  The broadest, multivendor platform support from one console and common
   data repository. In V1.0 the system manager sitting in front of a Windows
   NT console can drag and drop software upgrade packages to be installed on
   DEC OSF/1, NetWare, Windows, SunOS, OpenVMS, Windows NT, MS-DOS,
   Macintosh, OS/2, Windows for Workgroups, PATHWORKS, LAN Manager, ULTRIX,
   NT Advanced Server, and OpenVMS clusters across TCP/IP, DECnet, SNA,
   IPX/SPX, ISDN, and X.25 network environments. When the selected updates
   are completed, the updated inventory information can be viewed on the
   same console. In addition to hardware and software information,
   information on users, printer queues, licenses, and networks is
   collected.

Digital provides complete asset management, with a portfolio of value added
services and tools which deliver solutions addressing the asset management
problem in the legacy, LAN, and enterprise environments. POLYCENTER
AssetWORKS software is part of the Software Utility, which helps users
leverage entire software budgets and efficiently manage software assets from
acquisition through retirement.

BENEFITS

o  Users have access to the software they need, when they need it. They
   don't have to spend their time trying to manage their own systems, and
   departments don't need a "guru" to troubleshoot and lend assistance. The
   ability for the system manager to deploy standard "suites" of
   applications electronically to the desktop puts everything the user needs
   there.

o  System managers and LAN managers are relieved of tedious manual tracking,
   freeing them to focus on delivering technical consulting and back-end
   user support.

o  Remote control of PCs lets system managers diagnose and fix the problem
   without leaving their desks.

o  Software upgrades can be tested centrally and then scheduled for
   unattended deployment to remote sites, obviating expensive and unreliable
   "sneaker net." The hierarchical structure of POLYCENTER AssetWORKS
   software enables delegation of jobs as well as centralized administration
   with remote, local control.

o  POLYCENTER AssetWORKS software reduces help desk calls by ensuring
   complete, consistent software installations of the correct software
   versions on all target systems. Support headaches are minimized because
   system managers already know that the software "suites" work together and
   that everyone is at the same version of software.

o  Automated inventory features let system managers know where and how their
   computing assets are deployed, including what's changed or what's been
   added by users. Inventory is extensible and customizable. POLYCENTER
   AssetWORKS software not only tracks shrinkwrapped software, it also
   reports "homegrown" software applications developed to address business
   requirements.

o  POLYCENTER AssetWORKS software provides the tools to manage software like
   the corporate asset it is -- the ability to pool and share resources,
   recognize and remove unwanted software, and negotiate volume purchases
   with software vendors.

o  Automated configuration tools help control the ongoing costs associated
   with managing multivendor assets in a distributed computing environment,
   providing maximum productivity for the least cost.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

POLYCENTER AssetWORKS V1.0 will be available December 20, 1994 through local
Digital sales offices, service sales representatives, and Digital's business
partners. POLYCENTER AssetWORKS software extends Microsoft's Systems
Management Server with the capability for managing multivendor platforms.
The System Management Server product is a prerequisite for POLYCENTER
AssetWORKS.

Users only wishing to inventory and manage PCs should purchase System
Management Server. Users wanting management reports or wishing to add
support for OpenVMS, SunOS, DEC OSF/1, ULTRIX, DECnet, and PATHWORKS
products should purchase POLYCENTER AssetWORKS software. AssetWORKS software
works seamlessly with the System Management Server product, even if it was
purchased elsewhere and is already installed. Digital will resell System
Management Server (please refer to the "Microsoft's Systems Management
Server V1.0" article in this issue) as well as the POLYCENTER
AssetWORKS/System Management Server packages below.

POLYCENTER AssetWORKS software uses simple PC style packaging, including a
platform generic client. Users can aggregate the total number of
workstations to be managed and purchase the appropriate volume package to
achieve the most favorable discount.

System Management Server requires an user license for every machine to be
managed by the server. Digital offers packages including the System
Management Server user license with the POLYCENTER AssetWORKS agent license
as well as a combined POLYCENTER AssetWORKS/System Management Server
package. Also offered are POLYCENTER AssetWORKS only servers and agents for
users who may have purchased System Management Server elsewhere or who may
want to purchase POLYCENTER AssetWORKS software at a later time to enhance
their asset management solution.

