EISA Prestoserve NVRAM Option for DEC OSF/1

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Prestoserve DEC OSF/1 I/O performance enhancement for EISA bus based
   systems

o  Improves DEC OSF/1 system performance (including NFS servers) by reducing
   disk I/O

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

UNIX operating systems, including DEC OSF/1 systems, require a large amount
of disk I/O. This product off-loads much of this disk I/O overhead by
caching frequently written data blocks into non-volatile memory. The cached
data is held in NVRAM until peak system activity subsides, and is then
written to disk, thereby increasing overall system performance.

The PB2SX-AA option is an EISA Prestoserve (NVRAM) disk cache server
designed for use in EISA bus based DEC OSF/1 systems. The EISA Prestoserve
option has 1 Mbyte of non-volatile RAM. A lithium battery provides memory
retention with automatic switchover in the event of power failure.

BENEFITS

Prestoserve speeds up synchronous disk writes, including NFS (Network File
System) server access, by reducing disk I/O. Frequently written data blocks
are cached in non-volatile memory on this EISA option. The cached data is
then written to disk asynchronously as needed, or when the machine is idle.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The EISA Prestoserve NVRAM Option for DEC OSF/1 systems is available now.

Order No.        Description

PB2SX-AA	 EISA Prestoserve NVRAM Option for DEC OSF/1
		 with Prestoserve disk cache server software
		 (requires one EISA slot)

TECHNICAL DATA

o  Software Support -- The PB2SX is designed to operate with Digital's DEC
   OSF/1 operating system software, V2.0 and higher. Please note that
   AlphaServer 2100 products require DEC OSF/1 V3.0 release for PB2SX
   support.

o  Systems Support -- The PB2SX is supported on DEC 2000 Model 300 and 500
   systems and AlphaServer 2100 DEC OSF/1 systems. The configuration limit
   is one PB2SX option per system as defined by the Prestoserve software.

